WEBVTT

00:20.410 --> 00:23.000
- FIRST ASTRONOMICAL VELOCITY NEW
YEAR'S SHOW SUPER SUPERNOVA - DEC 31

00:20.410 --> 00:23.000
22:30 DOORS OPEN
23:00 SHOW STARTS
24:00 SHOW ENDS

00:56.030 --> 00:58.160
Baby, baby, baby

01:01.750 --> 01:04.210
Baby, baby, baby

01:04.750 --> 01:06.540
Sonico!

01:29.110 --> 01:34.070
Ryuusenkei o egaite hikaru
It shines, tracing a streamlined path

01:34.400 --> 01:36.700
Hitotsu no hoshi A single star

01:36.950 --> 01:39.910
(Hitotsu no hoshi)
(A single star)

01:40.120 --> 01:45.289
Ufugoe ageru, sono shunkan o
Those cries of birth, that's the moment

01:45.290 --> 01:47.580
Mitsumete hoshii
I want you to see

01:47.880 --> 01:50.459
(Mitsumete hoshii)
(I want you to see)

01:50.460 --> 01:52.710
Wasurete wa dame!
You mustn't forget'.

01:52.960 --> 01:55.340
Donna toki datte
Whenever, wherever

01:55.720 --> 02:00.430
Mirai wa bokura ni hohoenderu
The future is smiling on us

02:00.600 --> 02:01.970
Hop, step, jump!

02:02.100 --> 02:04.769
Baby, baby, baby, let's go!

02:04.770 --> 02:07.559
Kiseki no inochi, LET'S GO!
A miraculous life, let's go!

02:07.560 --> 02:10.190
Baby, baby, baby, let's go!

02:10.360 --> 02:12.820
Hikari yori mo hayaku
Faster than light

02:13.030 --> 02:15.610
Baby, baby, baby, let's go!

02:15.780 --> 02:18.410
Kiseki no inochi, LET'S GO!
A miraculous life, let's go!

02:18.570 --> 02:21.079
Baby, baby, baby, let's go!

02:21.080 --> 02:24.870
Chikyuu wa mawaritsuzukeru
The Earth can keep spinning

02:27.080 --> 02:28.920
Baby, baby

02:29.420 --> 02:33.670
Good evening, everyone!
We're First Astronomical Velocity!

02:41.470 --> 02:43.850
Good evening, everyone!

02:44.390 --> 02:46.310
We're the three-piece girl band...

02:47.350 --> 02:49.350
First Astronomical Velocity!

02:51.980 --> 02:58.950
We really want to thank all of you for coming out to
"Super Supernova," our New Year's countdown concert.

03:00.030 --> 03:03.410
Please, PLEASE stay and
have fun with us till the end!

03:05.410 --> 03:10.710
It's kind of a miracle we were even
able to have our show here tonight.

03:11.290 --> 03:13.040
Isn't that right, Suzu?

03:13.250 --> 03:16.340
Yes, absolutely right.

03:17.670 --> 03:20.720
And it's all Suzu's fault.

03:20.840 --> 03:22.720
Huh?

03:23.850 --> 03:26.930
Never mind that! We made
the show happen, right?

03:29.350 --> 03:35.940
There was a time we were ready to give up on this show.
But everyone from the Musatani Shopping District...

03:36.230 --> 03:39.740
The manager and everyone
at SuperNova night club...

03:40.070 --> 03:42.320
Aako from Beat On music studio...

03:42.620 --> 03:43.620
Ena!

03:43.700 --> 03:47.910
Everyone from Musasaka University's
band club... Yumi and Emi...

03:48.330 --> 03:52.960
We're able to play for you tonight
thanks to the help of all those people.

03:53.420 --> 03:55.500
Thank you all so much!

03:56.250 --> 04:01.760
It's with gratitude for you all, and the
whole world, that we sing this next song.

04:02.340 --> 04:03.340
This is...

04:04.050 --> 04:05.470
"Love the World"!

04:09.390 --> 04:10.480
Huh?!

04:10.940 --> 04:16.190
W-we don't have enough to pay for our
New Year's show? But why not, Suzu?

04:17.150 --> 04:22.449
But with Nico and me working in the
shopping district, and you at SuperNova,

04:22.450 --> 04:25.370
we should have covered the rental costs.

04:26.240 --> 04:30.580
I-I wanted a big audience for this one...

04:30.830 --> 04:33.460
So I booked Inokashira Park as our venue.

04:34.290 --> 04:37.129
And that took all of our money?

04:37.130 --> 04:40.800
No. I got a good price on an outdoor stage.

04:41.220 --> 04:42.760
So then why...?

04:43.090 --> 04:48.470
The truth is, since it was cheaper than I'd
thought, and it's an outdoor show and all...

04:48.890 --> 04:51.940
I rented a super-cool lighting rig.

04:52.440 --> 04:55.650
Then I hired a pro to operate it...

04:56.270 --> 04:59.940
But there was still the speakers
and the PA system to pay for...

04:59.941 --> 05:01.400
BILL

05:02.070 --> 05:04.280
And I just couldn't afford it.

05:05.280 --> 05:09.660
I'm sorry! Nico, Fuuri! I
got way too carried away!

05:13.120 --> 05:16.960
I have a few ideas, so
just give me a little time.

05:18.340 --> 05:20.710
We WILL do this show!

05:26.050 --> 05:27.320
PUB

05:27.321 --> 05:28.590
ZEPPELIN

05:35.730 --> 05:37.730
Oh, Sonico. Welcome back.

05:37.980 --> 05:39.570
It's cold today, huh?

05:42.070 --> 05:43.240
Sonico.

05:45.320 --> 05:46.660
Is something wrong?

05:53.120 --> 05:55.670
Um... Tomi, Kuni, Yasu!

05:57.130 --> 05:58.289
I need a favor!

05:58.290 --> 06:04.420
Won't you please help me... Rather, First
Astronomical Velocity? I can't do this alone!

06:06.260 --> 06:08.430
I don't know what's goin' on...

06:09.800 --> 06:12.810
But, Sonico, you and Leyla are our friends!

06:13.520 --> 06:15.600
Of course we're gonna help you!

06:15.850 --> 06:16.810
Count on it.

06:16.811 --> 06:19.980
I'll help as well, Sonico.

06:22.570 --> 06:24.150
Thank you so much!

06:24.490 --> 06:28.450
SHARE ONE DREAM, fushigi na chikara
Share one dream, a mysterious power

06:26.400 --> 06:28.450
The setup for your concert venue, huh?

06:28.660 --> 06:31.330
Wanna ask the younger
folks in the shopping district?

06:29.990 --> 06:31.739
Kitto DAY BY DAY
Surely, day by day

06:31.740 --> 06:35.160
They owe Sonico and her friends for
their help during the "Christmas war."

06:31.740 --> 06:35.959
Minna kara todoku POWER
You'll receive power from everyone

06:35.960 --> 06:38.329
And we'll need tents
for a live show, right?

06:36.580 --> 06:40.539
SHARE ONE DREAM, tsuyoku nareru yo
Share one dream, you can become stronger

06:38.330 --> 06:40.540
Let's borrow the ones we use for festivals.

06:40.540 --> 06:40.670
Let's borrow the ones we use for festivals.

06:40.671 --> 06:43.380
I'll ask the neighborhood
association about it.

06:42.130 --> 06:43.709
Motto DAY BY DAY
More, day by day

06:43.710 --> 06:46.260
And I'll reach out to the
neighborhood youngsters.

06:44.050 --> 06:47.680
Mae e susume! Bokura to
Move forward! With us

06:47.930 --> 06:49.470
Love the world

06:51.930 --> 06:54.640
Tomi... Kuni... Yasu...

06:55.140 --> 06:58.810
Grandma... Everyone! Thank you!

06:59.440 --> 07:01.359
Here's another way to say thanks!

07:01.360 --> 07:06.070
It's a new song we prepared just for today:
Seven-Colored Melody!

07:10.740 --> 07:12.910
Lend you some amps and speakers?

07:13.370 --> 07:15.500
Yes. And a PA, if you can.

07:16.620 --> 07:17.620
No problem.

07:18.460 --> 07:22.090
We're only open during
the day on New Year's Eve.

07:22.540 --> 07:25.880
You could borrow it later that afternoon.

07:26.130 --> 07:29.050
Still, you'd be doing your show
without rehearsing. That okay?

07:29.430 --> 07:31.849
It's more than enough!

07:31.850 --> 07:35.100
Oh? Well, I'll help out
behind the scenes, too.

07:32.220 --> 07:36.890
Tokimeki hazumu tokubetsu na jikan It's
a special time, my heart pounding excitedly

07:35.100 --> 07:35.770
Huh?

07:35.771 --> 07:36.890
You don't mind?

07:37.310 --> 07:38.230
Nope!

07:38.231 --> 07:41.770
Kiseki o okosu hikari to kage no naka Between
light and darkness, where miracles happen

07:41.771 --> 07:44.770
The truth is, I'd assumed you guys
would be doing your New Year's show here,

07:42.110 --> 07:45.750
Atarashii kyoku kanadetai, kimi to
I want to play a new song with you

07:45.751 --> 07:47.945
so now I've got nothing going on. Nothing!

07:47.946 --> 07:53.280
Kanjiru mama ni kono omoi nosete Putting
more into these emotions, I feel them

07:48.530 --> 07:49.530
U-um!

07:49.950 --> 07:52.910
If possible, please
let me help out as well!

07:53.580 --> 07:57.450
Ima kakinarase! SPEED o age
Strum the strings! Raise the speed!

07:53.700 --> 07:57.580
Speaking of, do you know how you're
getting the equipment to your venue?

07:57.581 --> 08:00.580
Kimi ni todoku made
Till they reach you

07:58.040 --> 08:00.039
Um, not yet.

08:00.040 --> 08:01.879
I thought as much.

08:01.880 --> 08:05.380
Nanairo ni kirameku senritsu
O shining, seven-colored melody

08:02.130 --> 08:03.750
Huh? E-Ena!

08:04.170 --> 08:05.380
Why are you...?

08:05.590 --> 08:07.880
Hatenaki sora e to
Stretch toward an endless sky

08:07.881 --> 08:10.840
This is a case. And where there's a case,
there is Ena Fujimi.

08:08.170 --> 08:10.970
Tsunagare, niji no you ni
Like a rainbow

08:11.680 --> 08:15.560
And a great detective
solves the case quickly!

08:12.800 --> 08:15.470
Boku wa boku de dekiru koto
I'll do what I can

08:15.760 --> 08:18.480
Soko kara hajimeru no sa
It starts from there

08:18.640 --> 08:19.140
Arata na mirai, ashita e
A new future, heading toward tomorrow

08:19.140 --> 08:20.140
Well, Suzu?

08:20.141 --> 08:22.900
Arata na mirai, ashita e
A new future, heading toward tomorrow

08:20.980 --> 08:22.270
H-how did you...?!

08:22.900 --> 08:24.110
- Well, all I can say is it's a gift from someone who wants to support your band—
- Arata na mirai, ashita e A new future, heading toward tomorrow

08:24.113 --> 08:29.320
Well, all I can say is it's a gift from
someone who wants to support your band...

08:30.450 --> 08:33.159
Way to go, Ena! You're the best!

08:33.160 --> 08:35.580
I give up! I give up!

08:38.500 --> 08:39.750
All right! All right!

08:42.370 --> 08:45.130
We've gotta set this up before the
sound system gets here.

08:42.960 --> 08:44.500
Jidai wa mawaru Times revolve

08:44.750 --> 08:49.460
Kibou mo zetsubou mo kurikaesareru
Hope and despair reoccur

08:45.500 --> 08:47.340
Let's give it our all, guys!

08:47.630 --> 08:48.630
Yeah!

08:49.010 --> 08:51.880
Good work, everyone.
We've brought some tea.

08:50.420 --> 08:52.590
Hikari to kage no naka
Between light and shadows

08:52.970 --> 08:57.510
Atarashii ippou, fumidaseru yuuki o!
A new step, get the courage to set forth!

08:54.510 --> 08:57.180
Thank you so much, everyone!

08:57.430 --> 08:58.470
No problem.

08:58.471 --> 09:03.810
Furikaerazu ni sono michi o zutto susume! Don't
look back, just head straight down that path!

08:58.970 --> 09:00.639
People help each other when they need it.

09:00.640 --> 09:02.060
Sonico!

09:02.980 --> 09:04.060
Aako!

09:04.150 --> 09:05.810
Kimi dake ja nai
You're not alone

09:06.650 --> 09:08.190
What are you doing here?

09:08.191 --> 09:11.280
Tsumazuitemo, saa, kao o agete Even
if you stumble, come on, raise your head

09:08.650 --> 09:12.200
You should've told me! I heard from
the manager at SuperNova.

09:12.490 --> 09:14.450
You don't have enough
equipment for your show?

09:12.530 --> 09:15.029
Nanairo ni kirameku senritsu
O shining, seven-colored melody

09:15.030 --> 09:17.280
I loaded up a bunch
of stuff from my studio.

09:16.240 --> 09:18.700
Te to te o tsunaide
Let's join hands

09:17.280 --> 09:18.700
You can use whatever you want.

09:18.910 --> 09:21.830
Hirogaru niji no you ni
Like a rainbow stretching outward

09:19.200 --> 09:21.329
A-are you sure?

09:21.330 --> 09:22.710
In return...

09:23.500 --> 09:26.040
I expect a POWERFUL concert!

09:23.500 --> 09:26.330
Chikara awase, dekiru koto
Join forces, do what you can

09:26.460 --> 09:27.250
Sure!

09:26.540 --> 09:29.170
Minna de mae o muite
Let's look forward, all of us

09:29.420 --> 09:34.470
Aruite yukou, ashita e
And walk toward the future

09:30.130 --> 09:32.130
A poster to advertise our show?

09:34.470 --> 09:37.350
Sorry, this was all I could do...

09:37.640 --> 09:40.810
Not at all. It's great, Fuuri!

09:44.100 --> 09:45.480
Thank you, Fuuri!

09:49.980 --> 09:50.780
Ciao!

09:50.781 --> 09:51.990
Ma'am?

09:52.280 --> 09:53.739
Wh-what can I...

09:53.740 --> 09:54.700
Don't you give me that!

09:54.701 --> 09:57.640
Hoshi no hikari yori mo
Even more than a star's light

09:57.641 --> 10:02.450
I heard you're short-staffed for your New
Year's concert. I came to see how I can help.

09:58.160 --> 10:03.579
Itsuka, itsuka kitto kagayaite
One day, one day it's sure to shine

10:03.580 --> 10:04.330
Yay!

10:04.540 --> 10:05.830
We're here, too!

10:05.831 --> 10:13.831
Nanairo ni kirameku senritsu
O shining, seven-colored melody

10:06.210 --> 10:08.250
Emi! And Yumi!

10:08.840 --> 10:12.420
We'll handle venue management,
ticket sales, or whatever!

10:17.050 --> 10:19.180
Hatenaki sora e to
Stretch toward an endless sky

10:19.390 --> 10:22.600
Tsunagare, niji no you ni
Like a rainbow

10:24.180 --> 10:26.810
Sekai ga hora, hohoenda
Look, the world has smiled

10:24.770 --> 10:27.059
B-broadcast on the Internet?

10:27.060 --> 10:29.145
Soko kara hajimaru no sa
It starts from there

10:29.146 --> 10:32.150
Right. We'll stream the
concert footage in real time.

10:32.151 --> 10:35.400
Arata na mirai, ashita e
A new future, heading toward tomorrow

10:32.480 --> 10:38.160
That way, even those who can't attend can
hear First Astronomical Velocity rock!

10:54.590 --> 10:57.010
Thank you, everyone!

10:58.970 --> 11:03.470
The year's almost over, so
let's race ahead at full power!

11:03.930 --> 11:05.810
And now, for the town I love...

11:06.310 --> 11:08.440
"Kichijoji Super Sonic"!

11:30.630 --> 11:34.550
Uh... Um, well... Let's see...

11:35.710 --> 11:39.930
Do... do you think you
could give us a minute?

12:00.780 --> 12:03.370
What?! You don't have a spare guitar?!

12:03.570 --> 12:04.910
S-sorry!

12:05.620 --> 12:08.159
Nico, get new strings on it, quick!

12:08.160 --> 12:10.289
Th-they're not here!

12:10.290 --> 12:11.290
Huh?!

12:11.920 --> 12:14.340
They must be buried somewhere.

12:15.670 --> 12:16.800
No way!

12:18.460 --> 12:25.010
Fuuri's buying us some time with her drum solo, but
there's only so long she'll be able to keep that up.

12:25.260 --> 12:27.270
They're gone! Where are they?!

12:31.770 --> 12:33.100
That sound...

12:40.610 --> 12:41.740
Grandma!

12:45.660 --> 12:46.660
How...?

12:46.830 --> 12:49.370
Why's that old lady so good?

12:50.080 --> 12:53.120
I haven't heard Leyla's guitar in ages.

12:53.420 --> 12:55.670
Still gets ya teary-eyed, don't it?

12:57.800 --> 13:01.340
Close your eyes and it all comes back, huh?

13:06.140 --> 13:08.180
She was our idol.

13:08.770 --> 13:10.480
No, not just that...

13:11.600 --> 13:13.690
She was our goddess.

13:21.740 --> 13:22.740
Sonico!

13:23.490 --> 13:24.490
Aako!

13:24.570 --> 13:25.739
I've brought help.

13:25.740 --> 13:29.240
Yup! Just leave the
guitar-fixing to ME, Sonico!

13:32.120 --> 13:33.710
Thank you so much!

13:45.380 --> 13:48.510
Okay! That does it! Here!

13:56.100 --> 13:57.150
Grandma!

13:58.230 --> 14:01.400
Sonico, I kept the stage warm for you.

14:01.730 --> 14:02.730
Good luck!

14:03.150 --> 14:05.780
Yeah! Thanks, Grandma!

14:15.500 --> 14:18.210
Sorry about that, but here we are.

14:18.920 --> 14:23.590
Lost time won't come back,
but we're First Astronomical Velocity.

14:24.050 --> 14:28.140
We'll break free of Earth's gravity
and fly at the speed of light!

14:28.470 --> 14:30.140
"Passion Rocket"!

14:39.360 --> 14:43.570
Hai-iro gakatta kyuukutsu na sora
A gray, oppressive sky

14:44.820 --> 14:47.860
Boku no mune o shimetsukeru
Squeezes my heart

14:47.990 --> 14:49.449
What's with you?

14:49.450 --> 14:53.700
We finally get a break after the end-of-year
rush, then you suddenly call me out for THIS?

14:54.120 --> 14:57.870
Well, at least we can avoid a sexual
harassment-fueled New Year's party.

14:58.120 --> 14:59.500
Sorry, Yuuko.

15:00.250 --> 15:04.880
Still, an indie rock show?
I didn't know you were into rock.

15:06.630 --> 15:08.470
Not really, but...

15:08.760 --> 15:11.929
I guess I owe them. I want someone
to have a copy of this...

15:11.930 --> 15:14.810
LITERATURE STAR
VOL 26 COLLECTED WORDS
OF NEW WRITERS
AWARD WINNERS

15:16.770 --> 15:20.190
I see. Your spring has
finally come, Sayaka!

15:20.690 --> 15:23.070
You can ask me for love advice anytime!

15:23.400 --> 15:25.569
I can't wait to see what this guy's like!

15:25.570 --> 15:28.170
You've got it all wrong!
I can't wait to see what this guy's like!

15:38.500 --> 15:41.540
Did your agency arrange this show?

15:43.840 --> 15:48.630
No. I just came to see
Sonico in action. And you?

15:49.380 --> 15:51.050
I'm a photographer.

15:51.680 --> 15:54.180
I go wherever there's
a good shot to be taken.

15:54.181 --> 15:57.139
Tobidashite kaze o kanjite
I run out the door, feel the wind

15:57.140 --> 15:58.480
Nice smile.

15:59.140 --> 16:06.400
Kimi ga iru kara boku wa hashiritsuzukeru
I'll keep on running because you're here

16:06.730 --> 16:13.740
I'd like Sonico's smile to reach as many
people as possible. That's my thinking.

16:06.940 --> 16:11.820
Habatake, sekai no hate de! Spread
those wings, to the ends of the Earth!

16:12.450 --> 16:15.080
Machiwabiteiru
I'm waiting impatiently

16:15.081 --> 16:17.935
Same here. I want to keep taking
pictures of that wonderful smile.

16:17.936 --> 16:19.000
Unmei no DOOR So knock

16:19.210 --> 16:21.670
Tatakunda On destiny's door

16:51.530 --> 16:56.700
First Astronomical Velocity has had
a lot of experiences this past year.

16:57.120 --> 17:02.250
Yup. Like the time your costume
melted off during a performance!

17:03.290 --> 17:05.580
Fuuri! You didn't have to mention that!

17:07.340 --> 17:11.420
How about the time we got chased by
neo-zombies on a luxury liner?

17:11.920 --> 17:13.260
Or that, either!

17:16.100 --> 17:21.099
Well, a lot has happened.
Things that were happy and a lot of fun...

17:21.100 --> 17:22.690
And some that weren't.

17:23.390 --> 17:26.230
But, I think they all go
toward making memories.

17:26.480 --> 17:28.600
It's because of you all that
I made those memories...

17:28.690 --> 17:32.530
And I'm grateful for my new friends.

17:33.240 --> 17:40.160
So, it's with all those
thoughts and memories...

17:41.830 --> 17:43.910
that we sing this song to you:

17:44.580 --> 17:46.960
"Love & Peace+."

18:05.060 --> 18:07.650
Daiji no koto wa Be sure to say

18:07.900 --> 18:11.940
Chanto tsutaete ne
The most important things

18:13.440 --> 18:20.490
Hitori dake nayande tamekondecha RAINY DAY If
you worry alone, keep it all in, it's a rainy day

18:21.790 --> 18:25.500
Me ni utsuru mono ga subete
I don't think everything

18:25.750 --> 18:29.540
Tadashii koto nante omowanai
That we see is valid

18:30.290 --> 18:37.970
Dakara sorezore no omoi o kotoba ni shite So take
those various sentiments and turn them into words

18:38.590 --> 18:42.390
Kokoro ni hana ga saku you ni
Like the smile that shows on your face

18:42.970 --> 18:46.810
Kimi ga egao de aru you ni
Like the smile that shows on your face

18:47.310 --> 18:51.230
Sekaijuu ga usotsuki demo
The world is full of liars

18:51.690 --> 18:55.320
Boku wa kimi o shinjiteru
But I believe in you

18:55.570 --> 18:58.660
LOVE to PEACE to ROCK-N-ROLL
Love and peace and rock-n-roll

18:59.660 --> 19:03.080
LOVE to PEACE to ROCK-N-ROLL
Love and peace and rock-n-roll

19:03.490 --> 19:06.830
SPICE ga hitsuyou ne
That's the spice that

19:07.210 --> 19:09.290
Kono sekai wa The world needs

19:22.220 --> 19:27.310
There's not much time left in the year.
Thirty more seconds, and it'll be over!

19:27.730 --> 19:29.940
Thanks for everything this year!

19:30.270 --> 19:33.270
We hope to have you as fans next year, too!

19:34.020 --> 19:39.200
Here's hoping you all
have a fantastic new year.

19:40.160 --> 19:44.830
Okay, let's start the countdown! Ten!

19:45.120 --> 19:46.120
Nine!

19:46.500 --> 19:47.500
Eight!

19:47.960 --> 19:49.080
Seven!

19:49.460 --> 19:50.460
Six!

